.TH "OFD" "8" "" "Onesimus 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus"
.SH NAME
ofd \- Onesimus File Daemon, a drop\-in replacement for the Bareos File Daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ofd
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B ofd
backs up and restores the files of a client on behalf of a Director. It
reads the Bareos File Daemon configuration (bareos\-fd.d) and speaks the
Bareos protocol to Directors and Storage Daemons; a TLS gRPC control
listener runs on the File Daemon port + 1000. Plugins are signed WASM
bundles (ofd\-plugin\-\fIname\fR packages).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-file " path"
Write the log to
.I path
as well (default
.IR /var/log/onesimus/ofd.log );
.B none
for no log file. Without the right to open it ofd warns and logs to
stderr only. Colour codes are written only when the log goes to a terminal
alone.
.TP
.BI \-c " path" "\fR, \fP\-\-config " path
Configuration file or directory. Default: /etc/bareos/bareos\-fd.d.
.TP
.BI \-d " level" "\fR, \fP\-\-debug\-level " level
Debug level.
.TP
.B \-f\fR, \fP\-\-foreground
Run in the foreground.
.TP
.BI \-u " user" "\fR, \fP\-\-user " user
Run as this user.
.TP
.BI \-g " group" "\fR, \fP\-\-group " group
Run as this group.
.TP
.B \-t\fR, \fP\-\-test\-config
Read the configuration and exit.
.TP
.B \-s\fR, \fP\-\-no\-signals
No signal handling (debugging).
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fP\-\-verbose
Verbose messages.
.TP
.BI \-\-grpc\-listen " address"
TLS gRPC control listener (default [::]:\fIport\fR+1000); BNET always
stays available.
.TP
.BI \-\-grpc\-cert " file" "\fR, \fP\-\-grpc\-key " file
PEM certificate and key for gRPC (default: generated in the working
directory).
.TP
.B \-\-disable\-grpc
Do not start the gRPC listener.
.TP
.BI \-\-check\-plugin " bundle"
Verify and initialize a signed WASM plugin bundle and exit, with
.BI \-\-plugin\-policy " file"
(public X.509 trust policy JSON) and optionally
.BI \-\-plugin\-check\-operation " profile"
(default backup).
.TP
.B \-\-discover\-podman
Read\-only discovery of container host UIDs via conmon; print JSON and exit
(with
.BI \-\-conmon\-executable " path"
for trusted conmon binaries, repeatable).
.SH SYSTEMD
.PP
The package installs
.B ofd.service
(user root,
.BR "ofd \-f \-c /etc/bareos/bareos\-fd.d" ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/log/onesimus/ofd.log
Log file (option
.BR \-\-log\-file ;
rotated by
.IR /etc/logrotate.d/onesimus\-ofd ).
.TP
.I /etc/bareos/bareos\-fd.d
Configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR odir (8),
.BR oconsole (1),
.BR bareos\-fd (8)
